Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||02-26-2001||12:00 AM||||Hey everyone.  I just moved to Indiana From Fla.  Its just a tad colder here than it was in jacksonville.  i hope there is as many avid fiero owners here as there was in jax.  i was lucky enough to get to drive the whole thing.....pulling a trailer.  ugh.  although my car did it just fine.  not a single problem except it was so windy in IN that i had to drive in 4th gear the whole time just to keep it at hwy speeds.  i averaged about  mpg.  i had a 4x8 uhaul trailer behind me. i couldnt even tell it was back there.  just slowed me down.  hehe that sucked.  but i still cruised at 80 most of the time.  maybe a little fast but i dont lke  sittin for so long.  i only saw 2 fieros the whole way.  both of them within a mile of each other. one was a maroon gt  parked on the side of the road and the other was a white coupe.  well i hope to find some fiero owners around here.  talk to you all later.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000001||rodmcneill||02-26-2001||12:06 AM||||Welcome to Indiana, it's nice in the Summer!||||reg||14
Z||000002||gabriel||02-26-2001||07:28 AM||||&gt;Its just a tad colder here than it was in jacksonville.<P>You will remember those words when it's 15 degrees and the Artic north wind is blowing that sleet in you face.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>My very good advice is to look toward some serious rustproofing/undercoating if ya wants that Fiero to live long & prosper ...||||reg||1
